WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:04.060
If you want to see my theory about the secret
behind this mysterious machine at the end

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:07.380
of the trailer, then stick around to the end
of this video.

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:11.980
(Intro)

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:15.220
Anything I mentioned in my previous Happy
Death Day videos won't be in this video, so

00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:19.529
if you don't know the meaning of these posters
and you want to relive the day you watched

00:00:19.529 --> 00:00:22.019
those videos, then check out this playlist.

00:00:22.019 --> 00:00:24.529
And obviously there will be spoilers for the
first movie.

00:00:24.529 --> 00:00:29.660
In those videos on the original film, I mostly
focused on the decorations on this side of

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:30.660
the room.

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:34.190
But there were a couple notable things to
catch my eye on the other side, such as these

00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:36.100
but I'll come back those later in the video.

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:38.140
First, I want to look at this poster.

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:40.149
It's the cover of a book called Pulse of Power.

00:00:40.149 --> 00:00:44.460
I haven't read the book myself, but here's
a summary I found on Google books.

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:46.359
Destiny is always a choice!

00:00:46.359 --> 00:00:48.870
Tia Stanton is not an ordinary woman.

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:52.430
Created from a mystical rite, she is birthed
into a world where chaos and organization

00:00:52.430 --> 00:00:57.350
run side by side; where monster and man live
in unison but rarely with recognition of each

00:00:57.350 --> 00:00:58.350
other.

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:02.210
Until the race begins -- a fight to gain access
to the pool of power lying beneath her hometown

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:03.569
of Greenwich, Connecticut.

00:01:03.569 --> 00:01:07.790
It coincides with her twenty-fifth birthday
and her last chance to accept the full mantel

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:09.079
of this supernatural power.

00:01:09.079 --> 00:01:13.900
There are a lot of parallels between the protagonist
Tia Stanton, and Tree Gelbman from Happy Death

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:14.900
Day.

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:18.430
They are both female protagonists with a supernatural
aspect in their respective stories.

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:22.710
Both have a major test of character that lands
on their birthday and both have the sole responsibility

00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:24.979
of overcoming their circumstances.

00:01:24.979 --> 00:01:28.330
Looking back to that shelf in Carter’s dorm
room, there is also a mini-basketball.

00:01:28.330 --> 00:01:34.770
There is also a basketball hoop on the back
of their door which can be seen more clearly

00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:35.909
in the first film.

00:01:35.909 --> 00:01:39.939
Remember, Christopher Landon has been planning
this sequel all along, so foreshadowing the

00:01:39.939 --> 00:01:43.630
fact that Carter and his roommate Ryan are
basketball fans may be related to the fact

00:01:43.630 --> 00:01:48.180
that Happy Death Day 2U has a scene taking
place at their college's basketball game.

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:51.300
And in the basketball scene, we get a bit
more info about the branding of their college

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:52.700
team The Babies.

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:56.500
They are playing a team called the Tritons
and losing pretty badly.

00:01:56.500 --> 00:02:00.090
Some of the team’s slogans seen in the stands
include Welcome to the Cradle, The Cradle

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:04.060
Will Rock, Babies Gonna Deliver, which, to
prevent any of you from ending up on the wooosh

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:07.909
subreddit, is a pun about babies being newborns
and newborns being found in the delivery room

00:02:07.909 --> 00:02:08.909
at a hospital.

00:02:08.909 --> 00:02:10.890
There's also a banner reading "Naptime for
Thurman".

00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:13.810
I'm guessing Thurman is probably the star
player of the Tritons.

00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:17.970
The one that interests me most though is this
one that says"Baby Gang".

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:20.700
Could this be a hint that there are multiple
killers?

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:24.640
We do see other shots in the trailer with
multiple baby masks, and even instances where

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:28.502
there are other baby masks in the room seeing
the violence happen to show that they are

00:02:28.502 --> 00:02:30.280
possibly affiliated.

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:33.150
It's also interesting because if you remember
last year when I went into the Happy Death

00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:37.110
Day maze at Halloween Horror nights, there
was a room with a bunch of those baby-mask

00:02:37.110 --> 00:02:41.580
killers, something that wasn't really a scene
in the first movie, unlike everything else

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:43.070
we saw in that maze.

00:02:43.070 --> 00:02:46.560
In addition to there possibly being multiple
killers who don the baby mask, it looks like

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:50.310
there will also be suspense about who the
actually killer is, and who is just wearing

00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:52.130
the mask because they're a fan of the team.

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:56.200
I spotted Ryan in the background in the crowd
with Tree and Carter after the game.

00:02:56.200 --> 00:03:00.440
He's also wearing black and it appears this
is shortly before they get chased by a baby-mask

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:01.440
with a black hoodie.

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:05.810
We don't have enough info for me to really
make any predictions, but I'm inclined to

00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:08.190
add him to my list of suspects.

00:03:08.190 --> 00:03:12.010
By the way, in this scene in the trailer where
Tree offers Ryan advice about being stuck

00:03:12.010 --> 00:03:14.230
in the time loop, she mentions the following.

00:03:14.230 --> 00:03:17.080
"I might be able to help with that.

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:18.730
I died 11 times."

00:03:18.730 --> 00:03:20.260
But hold on.

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:23.000
She only died 10 times in Happy Death Day.

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:27.670
That means she's already back in the time-loop
before this conversation takes place.

00:03:27.670 --> 00:03:32.090
To make matters more complicated, this isn't
the exact same day she re-lived before, because

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:36.970
in this timeline, there's also someone going
after Lori, the killer from the first movie.

00:03:36.970 --> 00:03:41.150
And speaking of that first movie, there are
of course, a few callbacks like this knife

00:03:41.150 --> 00:03:45.670
through the door during a kill, Tree's walk
of shame, a visit to the hospital ward and

00:03:45.670 --> 00:03:49.720
this scene with Tree skydiving in her underwear
(possibly a reference to the time Tree goes

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:53.760
nude during the first one) just to mess with
people because she knows the day will reset.

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:57.170
On the skydiving plane, there is a poster
briefly seen towards the front of the aircraft

00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:59.200
that has the words, like a leaf.

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:03.280
The quote is common cliche, and a metaphor
for helplessness, but in this case, may also

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:07.650
be a reference to a character from the TV
show Firefly whose catchphrase is, "I am a

00:04:07.650 --> 00:04:12.210
leaf in the wind, watch how I soar," which
has a bit of a different meaning in the content

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:16.919
of skydiving obviously, but could be representative
of the themes of Happy Death Day, since trees

00:04:16.919 --> 00:04:20.320
have leaves, and Tree is the name of the character
who is trying to take control and find the

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:22.979
better version of her life, as she says in
the trailer.

00:04:22.979 --> 00:04:25.449
"But now I'm living the better version of
my life."

00:04:25.449 --> 00:04:29.449
If you watched my Things You Missed in Happy
Death Day, one thing I talked about was how

00:04:29.449 --> 00:04:33.569
the street signs used as decorations throughout
the movie were symbols of the flow of time,

00:04:33.569 --> 00:04:37.180
and how the one-way sign seen at the end of
the film meant that now that Tree has broken

00:04:37.180 --> 00:04:40.949
the curse she won't have to go back to the
beginning of that day anymore, time will only

00:04:40.949 --> 00:04:42.540
flow in one direction.

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:46.539
In the trailer, we see that sign again, this
time through a mirror, meaning the only way

00:04:46.539 --> 00:04:51.039
to go for her now is backwards in time in
order to solve the puzzle yet again and break

00:04:51.039 --> 00:04:52.039
the curse.

00:04:52.039 --> 00:04:54.770
This time, it seems like there's more to it
than just that and it has something to do

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:56.009
with this machine.

00:04:56.009 --> 00:04:59.520
If we quickly rewind to the beginning of the
trailer, there are a couple of books on this

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:04.479
shelf on the topics of biochemistry and molecular
cloning, and in the trailer after firing up

00:05:04.479 --> 00:05:09.850
this machine, Ryan can be seen briefly coming
face to face with himself.

00:05:09.850 --> 00:05:13.830
Could this have something to do with the fact
that after each day is reset, Tree's body

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:18.569
is unharmed, but her memories of the previous
day are somehow transferred to the new body?

00:05:18.569 --> 00:05:23.600
Will Happy Death Day 2U finally explain why
Tree is stuck in this loop in the first place?

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:27.320
If this trailer is any indication, we'll be
learning a lot more about the logistics of

00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:29.240
the time travel in this universe.

00:05:29.240 --> 00:05:33.130
Now when I gave the DeadTalk about Happy Death
Day 2U, I predicted that the new time loop

00:05:33.130 --> 00:05:37.740
would take place on Valentine's Day and the
2U was a reference to those candy hearts.

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:41.789
We now know this not to be the case, however,
my new theory on “2U” is that it's a reference

00:05:41.789 --> 00:05:45.259
to the passive aggressive language Tree and
her sorority use to communicate with each

00:05:45.259 --> 00:05:50.180
other, as seen in the first movie.

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:55.680
*music*

00:05:55.680 --> 00:06:01.760
Finally, there's one pretty creepy thing you
might have missed in the title animation,

00:06:01.780 --> 00:06:07.560
the face of the killer's mask is reflected
in the knife.

